  "producer_and_algorithm_review": [
    "Full plan recompilation owned fresh operations but retained stale root ranges and scalar leaf batch classifications. CPU regressions and actual Metal pixel comparisons reproduced both failures before production edits.",
    "The previous container collector silently skipped a multibatch leaf and chose a later scalar batch. A separate CPU and Metal regression reproduced the wrong insertion order before replacing that collector.",
    "Central full-plan installation now replaces all leaf classifications, actual root operation ranges and empty-branch membership together. Fragment installation removes obsolete scalar entries for multibatch leaves.",
    "Root ranges now come from one traversal of the current plan and retained ownership; per-root temporary command compilation and three obsolete owner-offset helpers are deleted.",
    "Insertion batch reuse follows actual adjacent execution runs through flattened groups; layers and nonplain leaves stop the search. Empty content/mask branches retain independent batch IDs. A per-update memo avoids quadratic walks across a newly inserted run.",
    "The first conservative whole-container eligibility implementation broke an existing expanding-clip delta-sharing test. It was rejected in favor of adjacent-run eligibility, which preserves that test and a 1024-leaf bulk insertion contract.",
    "The original root-reparent regression now starts with three draws so arena compaction cannot hide stale scalar metadata. Same-length repeated content revisions exercise the noncompacting path.",
    "Final review checks 128 layer-kind/empty-child transitions, non-tail removal, immutable older plans, all five new Metal pixel regressions, and independent empty mask branches. No additional likely bug was found within this implementation scope.",
    "Remaining range/plan presence substitutes and offscreen shape eligibility require a separate producer/caller proof; real Windows/Vulkan and ShaderTools execution remain pending."
  ],
